// Crusaders Mainframe — paying for somebody else's court, at the box (D10).
//
// THE FLOW, AS THE FOUNDER SPECIFIED IT
// -------------------------------------
//   scan -> press the booked court's button -> the glass asks
//   `CT2 BOOKED / PAY 50cr? / PRESS CT2 TO PAY` -> press it again -> paid.
//
// Two presses and two calls to `POST /api/v1/device/pay-for`: the first with
// `confirm:false`, which moves no money and returns the price the glass will
// ask about; the second with `confirm:true`, which echoes that price's LABEL so
// the member pays exactly what they agreed to or nothing (`price_changed`).
// ONLINE ONLY — the box knows neither the price nor who has paid what, and a
// guess at either is a member charged for something the club did not sell.
//
// WHEN THE BOX ASKS AT ALL
// ------------------------
// Only for a court this box believes is taken NOW — its roster holds an open
// booking on that relay, or the relay is lit — by a member who scanned. Any
// other court press is the walk-up choice it always was, and so is every
// answer that is not a decision: a server that has never heard of pay-for
// answers 404, and a box flashed before its server was upgraded must behave
// exactly as the box before it did. `not_booked` is the same: the court was
// free after all, so the press was a walk-up.
//
// THE NONCE
// ---------
// Fresh per quote, and the confirm carries the quote's. A confirm that got no
// decision — no connection, a 5xx, a 429, a 200 that could not be read — keeps
// the quote and its nonce armed, so pressing again retries the SAME payment
// and the server answers with the first one (`replayed:true`) rather than
// charging twice. The walk-up nonce's rule, for the walk-up's reason.
//
// SPLIT BOOKINGS
// --------------
// Refused by the server (`split_booking`) and shown as `SPLIT BOOKING / PAY IN
// APP`: each player's share is theirs to pay in the app, and a box that could
// take one member's credit for everybody's share is a box that settles a debt
// nobody agreed to.
//
// No Arduino headers, no heap, no String. Compiles for Xtensa and the host.

